// s12 MLS groups (MLS GUI batch M2, fixtures F2-1 to F2-10, and batch M3,
// fixtures F3-1 to F3-13). The groups are served by the handlers `mock_mls`
// and `mock_mls_admin` (crates/ramflux-desktop-test), not by the timeline:
// this file only sets the account up. The handlers are active only while this
// scenario is loaded, and count every `mls_group.*` call (the developer panel
// shows "mock calls: <method> N").
//
// How to reach each fixture (Groups route in the rail):
//   F2-1  Groups list: 120 groups in three pages of 50 (cursors l2, l3); page 2
//         repeats one group with a newer time. "Design" (owner, 12 members,
//         1 agent), "Neighbours" (member, 987), "Book club" (admin, 3,
//         catch-up spinner). Scroll to the end.
//   F2-2  Open "Neighbours", Members: 5 pages, 4 agents, one "You", 30 members
//         with no name. Page 3 fails once (host_unreachable): Try again. Type
//         in the search field: the remaining pages load.
//   F2-3  Open "Design" and scroll to the top: 260 posts, a deleted one, a
//         membership row of 15 joins, a name change, an undone change, an
//         unknown kind, and the floor line.
//   F2-4  Open any group and send 6 messages: sent; queued (catching up, then
//         sent by an event); delayed for privacy (then failed by an event);
//         rate limited (the composer is off for 20 s, then Retry works);
//         too large (Retry); an unknown state (queued).
//         The first send is also repeated by a `post` event: no extra row.
//   F2-5  Join with a link (group list, link button): rfinv-joined,
//         rfinv-admin (pending), rfinv-online (pending, then joined after
//         5 s), rfinv-slow (joined after 4 s), rfinv-down (host_unreachable),
//         rfinv-unknownreason (refused "banana"), and one refusal each:
//         rfinv-refused-<link_invalid|invite_expired|invite_invalid|group_full|
//         queue_full|request_expired|already_member|rate_limited>. A link of
//         513 characters or with a space fails the local check: no call.
//   F2-6  New group, then the invite panel (link, Copy link, presets, New link,
//         the list with a revoked and an expired invite). Revoke answers after
//         2 s. A name with the word "refuse" is refused (tier_unavailable).
//   F2-7  Open "Design": its first refresh brings a removal, a ban, a role
//         change, a device added (not shown) and a settings row (approval
//         off), 1.5 s apart. Open "Book club": 3 s after its first refresh
//         this account is removed: the chat becomes read only.
//   F2-8  Leave: "Design" (owner) answers owner_protected; any other group
//         answers committed, then a membership event drops it from the list.
//   F2-9  "Scale test": 1000 members and 20,000 posts, generated per page.
//   F2-10 Delete for everyone on an own posted message (send one first):
//         "Deleting..." for 2 s, then the tombstone (an event repeats it once).
//         The second delete of the session answers not_author.
//
// M3 (admin and edge states). Opening a group asks for a refresh: the FIRST
// refresh of a group brings its M3 timed events (below); the SECOND one (press
// Refresh again, at least 5 s later) brings the F2-7 news of Design and Book
// club, so the two walks do not trample each other (F2-7 now needs two
// refreshes). The list keeps its 120 rows: five fillers became the M3 groups
// "Queue", "Open house", "Late catch-up", "Catch-up zero" and "Stale head",
// which sit right after "Design". Quotas and privacy delays are real now
// (Design: 60 of 500 posts and 2 of 20 commits; Neighbours: first day, 3 of
// 20, privacy delay armed; Scale: privacy ETA 2 minutes after the start).
// Design's roster: Ana and Chen are admins; Ben, Scout (agent), Dana and Eve
// are members. Book club has 6 members (Ana is member 3, Chen member 4).
// Head commit of Design: the name change at 250 (older membership row at 240)
// until the F2-7 news add newer commits.
//   F3-1  Design, group info, "Join requests": 7 rows (Ana, Ben, Chen, Dana,
//         Eve, Scout, one with no name), then Fay arrives by event 4 s after
//         the first listing (once). Approve Ana: committed, joined row after
//         1 s. Approve Ben: request_not_found. Decline anyone: declined after
//         1 s. Approve Dana: paced for 5 s; Dana expires 30 s after the
//         first listing. Approve Eve: the reply takes 3 s (close the screen
//         at once, reopen). Counters: approve 4, decline 1.
//   F3-2  Queue, "Join requests": 200 rows and a cursor, then 230; page 2
//         fails once (host_unreachable), "Try again" loads it.
//   F3-3  Design, Members: Make Ben admin (his `membership` event arrives
//         0.5 s BEFORE the reply), Make Chen member, Remove Dana (reply
//         after 3 s), Ban Eve. The owner row and your own row have no menu.
//         (A removal of the owner row cannot be sent: the policy hides it.)
//   F3-4  Book club, Members (this account is an admin): Ana, a plain member,
//         offers Remove and Ban; Remove Ana answers not_admin{required:
//         admin} and the next group read says this account is a member.
//   F3-5  Design: Remove Dana (3 s), then try Ban Eve and Approve Fay.
//   F3-6  Design, Group settings: rename, a 65-character name, an unchanged
//         name, approval off (confirmation with the hint; settings event and
//         the admission warning follow), approval on. Neighbours, info: pick
//         each notification mode (None fails with a generic error).
//   F3-7  Book club, first refresh: catch-up progress 0 to 120 for 2 s, idle
//         after 5 s; Skip answers after 3 s. "Late catch-up": Skip answers
//         after 3 s and an idle event arrives 1 s after the call (the reply
//         changes nothing). "Catch-up zero": the total is 0 (indeterminate).
//   F3-8  Design, first refresh: fork_alarm, rejoin_needed for pruned,
//         gate_rejected, apply_failed, welcome_expired, state_lost and an
//         unknown reason, undecryptable (12 from 140), admission_needs_online,
//         host_unusual, head_commit_rejected (250) and an unknown code, each
//         active 3 s then cleared, 4 s apart; at the end three stay (fork,
//         undecryptable, host_unusual: two banners and "+1"). A group read
//         issued while fork_alarm is active is answered after it is cleared
//         and still lists it (the stale read). Neighbours (member), first
//         refresh: head_commit_rejected, which a member never sees.
//   F3-9  Design (post and commit quota lines), Neighbours (first-day line,
//         privacy row), Scale (privacy ETA). Send a message: the line changes
//         only after the next group read.
//   F3-10 Design, history: "Undo this change" on the head commit only;
//         committed then a void row. "Stale head": Undo is refused with
//         void_not_head (head 252) and the newer commit arrives. The
//         head_commit_rejected banner action opens the same confirmation.
//   F3-11 Book club, Members: Remove Chen (reply after 3 s); 1 s after the
//         call this account is removed (read only).
//   F3-12 Lock the app while Approve (Design, 3 s) or Skip (Book club, 3 s)
//         runs, and unlock after 5 s: nothing survives. A second mock
//         account is not offered: the mock source serves one MLS handler.
//   F3-13 "Open house" (admin, approval off): admission banner and info row
//         with "Get invite link" and "Open agents". The requester side is
//         the M2 link rfinv-online.
#![enable(implicit_some, unwrap_variant_newtypes)]
(
    name: "s12_mls_groups",
    description: "MLS groups: list, members, history, send states, join, invites, leave and delete on the mock",
    timeline: [
        (0, SourceStatusChanged(Connected)),
        (0, ListingsLoaded([Nodes, Accounts, Contexts, Contacts, Objects, Approvals])),
        (0, AccountUpdated(id: "local", label: "Local", lock_state: Unlocked, self_participant_id: "p-me")),
        (0, ParticipantUpserted(id: "p-me", kind: Human, display: "Alex Moreau")),
    ],
    responses: [],
)
